<title>GREECE: GREEK INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 0.9PCT YR/YR IN JULY.</title>
<headline>GREEK INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 0.9PCT YR/YR IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's industrial production rose provisionally by 0.9 percent year-on-year after a 1.4 percent rise in June and manufacturing output was unchanged year-on-year in July, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.  </p>
<p>The increase in July industrial production was mainly due to a rise of 7.0 percent year-on-year in mining output and 3.9 percent pick up in electricity-gaslight output, the NSS said.  </p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	 JULY 96*  JUNE 96** JULY 95</p>
<p>    Percent change(yr/yr)	0.9%	1.4%	1.8%</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	   114.0     112.7     112.9</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING OUTPUT    JULY 96*  JUNE 96** JULY 95</p>
<p>    Percent change(yr/yr)	0.0%	0.3%	2.1%</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	   104.0     104.4     104.0</p>
<p>*  an asterisk indicates provisional data</p>
<p>** two asterisks indicate revised data</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
